      "side": 1,
      "message": "Regarding the single assignment, the rx buffer needs to be cast as a struct pointer before dereferencing. This assignment works for me\n `pe[port].partner_rmdo \u003d *((struct rmdo *) rx_emsg[port].buf);`\n\nI think the buffer here is big-endian. As you mentioned we wanted bytes 2 and 3, but rx_emsg[port[.buf is pointing to byte 0. The data offset is used to copy bytes 2-3 instead of 0-1. Either way, I added the reserved field to the rmdo struct so now the assignment works with no offset. \n\nFWIW To test this, I\u0027m printing out the partner_rmdo fields from `pe_clear_port_data` right before clearing the parnter rmdo when a device is detached. I\u0027m using a 140W USB-C power adapter from Apple with EPR support which requires USB PD Rev 3.1. Here is what I am getting.\n\n\nEC log over Suzy Q\n\u003e [72.822087 Ramp p2 st5 3000mA 3000mA]\n\u003e [73.926394 RMDO Major Rev: 3]\n\u003e [73.926745 RMDO Minor Rev: 1]\n\u003e [73.927061 RMDO Major Ver: 1]\n\u003e [73.927379 RMDO Minor Ver: 0]\n\u003e [73.929457 C2: Unattached.SNK]",
